@startuml 06-media-state
' ============================================================
'  Media attachment lifecycle — persisted, crash-recoverable
' ============================================================

title Media Attachment — Persisted State Machine

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"

[*] --> captured : row written\n**before** any processing

captured --> compressing : worker picks up
compressing --> ready : encode + thumbnail ok
compressing --> failed : encode error

failed --> compressing : retry (max 3)
failed --> [*] : user discards

ready --> uploading : «deferred — backup phase»
uploading --> uploaded : remote_url set
uploading --> ready : transfer interrupted\n(upload_offset retained)
uploaded --> evicted : storage budget,\noriginal removed,\nthumbnail retained

evicted --> uploaded : re-fetch on demand

state "recovery on launch" as recovery
captured --> recovery : app killed mid-flight
compressing --> recovery : app killed mid-flight
recovery --> compressing : output missing → re-enqueue
recovery --> ready : output present → reconcile

note right of recovery
  OrphanSweeper reconciles DB rows
  against the filesystem at every launch.
  Files with no live row are deleted;
  rows with no output are re-enqueued.
end note

note bottom
  States after **ready** are greyed in the first cut —
  no backend, so nothing uploads. The column exists
  so the transition is additive later.
end note

@enduml


@startuml 07-data-model
' ============================================================
'  Domain / persistence entity relationships
' ============================================================

title Data Model — Entities & Sync Primitives

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #444444
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}
hide circle

class SyncPrimitives <<abstract>> #FFFDF0 {
  id : TEXT «UUIDv7, client-generated»
  user_id : TEXT = 'local'
  created_at : INTEGER «UTC epoch ms»
  updated_at : INTEGER
  deleted_at : INTEGER «tombstone»
  sync_state : INTEGER
  server_rev : INTEGER
  device_id : TEXT
}

note right of SyncPrimitives
  Present on **every** synchronisable table
  from commit one. BaseDao enforces
  `deleted_at IS NULL` on reads and bumps
  `updated_at` on writes.
end note

class WorkoutSession {
  started_at : INTEGER
  ended_at : INTEGER
  --
  local_date : TEXT «04:00 boundary»
  tz_offset_min : INTEGER
  --
  workout_type : TEXT
  title / notes : TEXT
  perceived_effort : INTEGER
  status : TEXT «planned|in_progress\n|completed|skipped»
}

class ExerciseLog {
  order_index : INTEGER
  set_index : INTEGER
  reps : INTEGER
  weight_kg : REAL «always SI»
  duration_sec : INTEGER
  distance_m : REAL
  rpe : REAL
  is_warmup : INTEGER
  rest_sec : INTEGER
}

class Exercise <<catalogue>> {
  name : TEXT
  category : TEXT
  primary_muscle : TEXT
  equipment : TEXT
  is_custom : INTEGER
}

class MediaAttachment {
  media_type : TEXT
  relative_path : TEXT «NEVER absolute»
  thumb_rel_path : TEXT
  mime_type / size_bytes
  width / height / duration_ms
  checksum_sha256 : TEXT
  capture_state : TEXT
  remote_url : TEXT «null in first cut»
  upload_state / upload_offset
}

class HealthSnapshot {
  local_date : TEXT
  window_start / window_end
  --
  steps / active_kcal / total_kcal
  calorie_basis : TEXT
  distance_m
  avg_hr / peak_hr / resting_hr
  zone_model_version : INTEGER
  zone_seconds_json : TEXT
  sleep_minutes
  coverage : REAL
  --
  source_id : TEXT
  source_package : TEXT
  source_record_id : TEXT
  source_modified_at
  ingested_at
}

class SourcePriority <<config>> {
  metric : TEXT
  source_id : TEXT
  rank : INTEGER
}

class HabitDefinition {
  name : TEXT
  cadence : TEXT
  target_count : INTEGER
  target_days_json : TEXT
  grace_days : INTEGER = 1
  active_from / active_to
}

class SyncCursor <<operational>> {
  source_id : TEXT «PK»
  cursor : TEXT
  last_success_at : INTEGER
  consecutive_failures : INTEGER
}

SyncPrimitives <|-- WorkoutSession
SyncPrimitives <|-- ExerciseLog
SyncPrimitives <|-- MediaAttachment
SyncPrimitives <|-- HealthSnapshot

WorkoutSession "1" *-- "0..*" ExerciseLog
WorkoutSession "1" *-- "0..*" MediaAttachment
ExerciseLog "1" o-- "0..*" MediaAttachment
ExerciseLog "*" --> "1" Exercise
WorkoutSession "1" o-- "0..1" HealthSnapshot : resolved view
SourcePriority ..> HealthSnapshot : ranks per metric

note bottom of HealthSnapshot
  **One row per day PER SOURCE**, not one per day.
  UNIQUE(source_id, source_package, source_record_id)
  is the dedup mechanism. SnapshotResolver picks the
  winner per metric — today always the only row.
end note

note bottom of ExerciseLog
  One row **per set**. Enables SQL progression
  queries and per-row conflict resolution later;
  a JSON blob would force document-level LWW.
end note

@enduml
